WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.901
-Paris!
-Hello.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.901
What's up, New York?!
-Yeah!

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.334
Welcome back.
The memoir's out tomorrow.

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:12.033
I want to get to this.
I want to talk about

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:13.400
the last time
you were on our show,

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.067
which I'm so psyched
every time you come on.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.400
It's always great.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.801
Last time,
do you remember what happened?

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:19.000
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.234
You -- commercial came,
and someone ran out.

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:24.701
Was it your mom?
-Yes.

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:26.000
-Your mom ran out and goes,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.200
"Paris, you're wearing
two different shoes."

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.667
-Mm-hmm.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.734
-During the whole interview.

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.167
And you didn't know.
I didn't know.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.133
No one said anything.
But here's the picture of you

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.901
before -- before you changed.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.601
This is during
one of our interviews.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:40.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.634
I -- I have a close-up
of just the shoes there,

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:44.968
just so we know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.934
-I don't know how I, like,
didn't notice that,

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.234
because one is, like,
all crystallized

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.801
and one is, like, nude.
-Did anyone think

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.767
that you were doing this
on purpose,

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.634
like it's a style choice?
-They did.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.100
People were like,
"Who is the designer?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.334
That's so cool."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:01.334
-That's so funny.
That's so good.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:02.734
But your mom came out
and straightened it out.

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:03.834
And so, you changed shoes.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.000
But I just wanted
to remind that.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.567
That made me laugh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:08.501
-Only me.
-Only you.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.734
This is the greatest thing
to ever happen to you

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.634
right here, pal.
You became a mom.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:16.601
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.501
He is such an angel.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:20.501
-How is he?
-He's the best.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.434
He's the cutest, sweetest.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.067
I'm just so obsessed with him.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.367
My heart feels
like it's gonna explode.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.501
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:27.701
-And do you just stare at him
when he --

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:28.901
-Stare at him.
-Right?

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.133
-Yes.
-That's all you do.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.601
You just go, "Oh, my God.
You're a perfect baby."

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.300
-It's the best.
-It's the best thing.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.934
And mom, Kathy,
is loving being grandma?

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.267
-Yes.
-Yeah, I could just imagine.

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.400
-Obsessed. Just showing up
all the time, unannounced.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.968
-Unannounced, yeah.
-She's, like, in there.

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.167
I'm like, "Mom,
when did you get here?"

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.300
She's like,
"Oh, I've been here for hours."

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.968
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, just waiting for you

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:47.200
to -- yeah, I got to wait
for the baby to wake up.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.734
Now -- you being a D.J.,
I'm assuming you have

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.367
a good playlist for the baby.

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.033
-Yes, of course.
-You do?

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:55.934
-Mm-hmm.
-What is baby into now?

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:58.968
-Well, I actually sang his
favorite lullaby is my song

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.767
"Stars are Blind."
-Really?

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.534
-Mm-hmm, yes.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:04.501
He has good taste in music.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:06.234
By the way,
you were great with Miley.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:07.934
-Thank you.
-That was fantastic.

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.067
-I love her so much.
She's so cool.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.367
-No, you can't beat Miley Cyrus.

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.334
But that was such a surprise.

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:13.734
I had no idea
you were gonna come out

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:15.067
and rock it out and do "Stars."

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.033
She's a fan of the song?
-Yes.

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:18.300
-I love her.
-I love her.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.834
-Dude, you guys together.
Yeah.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.868
-She is epic.
-That was awesome.

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:25.334
Let's talk about --
you have a memoir.

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.367
It's out tomorrow.
This is a big deal.

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:31.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:34.534
-When did you realize that you
were ready to write a memoir?

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:36.901
Was it the doc?
-Definitely the documentary.

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:40.100
That was the first time
that I actually got real

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.567
and started just thinking about
so many things

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:44.767
I'd went through in my life.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:48.400
-And it was just time,
I feel that, to tell my truth.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.868
-Yeah.
It's -- It gets --

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.601
the struggle story's in there,

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:54.767
and it gets dark
at certain points.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.601
But there's funnier,
lighter moments

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.901
and things in here that I --
that I never knew about you.

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:02.033
But I think this is,
for one example,

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.501
you like to do
prank phone calls?

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:04.868
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:06.067
-I didn't know this about you.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.534
You have a separate phone
just for pranking people?

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.767
-I do.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:12.667
-Now, how did you do it?

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:13.968
And where did you learn
to prank phone call?

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:15.400
Was it something you did
in high school?

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.100
-My mom taught me.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.534
-Your mom pranks people?

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:21.300
-She's the queen of prank calls.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.901
She is so good at it.
-Really?

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.968
-Yes.
-And how do you all react?

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.133
Do you hear on the other line,
or pick up when she calls,

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.133
or speaker phone?
-We do it at her house, like,

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:30.968
usually during parties,
like, at the end.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:32.801
Like, we'll all get together
in the room and just, like,

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.334
have a prank-calling
after-party.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.534
-Oh, my God.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.834
-And when you do it,
do you change your voice at all?

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:43.400
-"Yes, my name is Phyllis,
and I like to smoke the cigs,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.067
and I would love to move into
your apartment, darling."

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.067
-Oh, my God.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.868
-I'm just --
"I like to smoke the cigs."

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:51.000
-Yes, I don't know.
Someone --

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.033
-Why not do that?
I love learning that stuff,

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:54.801
because it's funny, it's light.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.567
But you always
had a good sense of humor.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:59.501
And, also, your business brain
is phenomenal...

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:00.767
-Thank you.
-...to learn about.

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:02.334
And you learn about this.

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:05.667
I also will say,
it does get very dark,

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.868
for people that
don't know you, know you.

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:09.734
-Yeah.
-You kind of are in shock,

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.234
and you go like, "Wow.

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:13.567
I didn't realize
you went through this."

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.567
And I'm happy
that you're telling your story.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:19.033
But this is -- a lot of stuff
happened to you as a teenager.

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:22.901
And you've actually taken it
to -- to -- to Congress.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:25.567
-Yeah. We've changed laws
in eight states so far

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:26.968
and all the way in Ireland.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:29.901
Thank you.
Yes.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:33.534
And now we're going back to D.C.
in April to introduce

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:35.634
our new bill
to make this federal.

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:39.601
-Come on. This is --
You are so fascinating.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.467
Congrats on this.
-Thank you.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:43.267
-Congrats on this,
and congrats on this, too.

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:44.534
-Yes.
-I mean, come on.

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:46.434
That's -- it's really
the best thing ever.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.434
-My two babies.
-Paris Hilton, everybody!

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:51.767
"Paris: The Memoir"
is out tomorrow.

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.534
Pick it up online,
go to Barnes &amp; Noble,

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:54.968
wherever books are sold.

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:56.300
We'll be right back
with Collin Morikawa.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.801
Stick around, everybody.

